// WHAT THE ATLAS ATTRIBUTES TO WHICH SPECIMEN, AS ROWS: this E1 part was seen in this frame at this box.
// It is the roster the marking mints (product.electrical.identification only_reading, no_dissent,
// prefer_checkable) check a reading's own sighting against. A reading's sighting is the CLAIM; this is the
// independent attribution, generated from the receipts and never from the readings, so a reading cannot
// attribute its own evidence.
//
// GENERATED by gunbc-private p4261/e1-atlas-handoff, docs/plans/2026-11-03-p4261-e1-atlas/scripts/gen_e1_board_sightings_dag.py
// at 2d9f1424c212; do not hand-edit. Reads per_photo_readings.jsonl, per_photo_readings_sd_2026-11-03.jsonl and per_photo_readings_sd_2026-11-06.jsonl
// (E1 frames only), the DesignatorReading rows of product.p4261.e1_b, and the digests of
// product.p4261.e1_photographs.
//
// THE RULE. A row per distinct (designator, frame digest, box) that a receipt item states for a designator
// the board's DesignatorReading rows name exactly once. A box is the receipt's own: a structured `bbox`
// field, or one of two coordinate shapes inside its `location` text ('x<n>-<n> y<n>-<n>' and
// 'orig <n>-<n> x <n>-<n>'); anything else is not a box and is not guessed. Each row's `box_source` says
// which, and a text-parsed box carries the receipt's exact string. A `location` string can state more than one
// box (a package and its label); every box it states is a row, because the receipt does not say which is the
// marking, so this roster attributes "seen here", never "this is the marking" -- the reading's claim about
// WHICH box is its marking is not checked here.
//
// SPECIMEN SPELLING. Specimens are spelled with e1_component (product.p4261.e1_design), never by importing
// e1_b: e1_b hands this roster to the marking mints, so this module cannot import it. That the designator
// below is the one the board's DesignatorReading rows give that specimen is therefore NOT structural; it is
// audited by the witness that imports both (product.test.claim.product.p4261_marking_witness).
//
// COUNTS (from this run): 1148 rows, of which 489 from a structured bbox and 659 from parsed location text.
// NOT EMITTED, by reason: 260 x no DesignatorReading; 516 x receipt item states no box in the receipts' grammar.

